   "widgets_values": [
    "Picture 2 shows the exact title lettering \"THE COLOSSUS PASS\". Add exactly this lettering to the film frame in Picture 1 as monumental letters deeply carved into the ancient weathered rock face, as if cut by a lost civilisation. Copy the letters from Picture 2 precisely: the same words, the same spelling (T-H-E C-O-L-O-S-S-U-S P-A-S-S), the same order and line layout, appearing only once. Place the lettering on a real surface in the scene where it would truly exist, such as a rock face, wall, building or sign (only light-based lettering may float in the air), large and clearly readable, following that surface's perspective, light and weather. Keep everything else in the frame unchanged: same composition, framing, subjects and colours. No other text."
